Well, I just recently received Nethack 3.1.0, and played for a couple hours
yesterday.  Once, I saved out, ate supper, and came back.  Low and behold,
my save file won't start up!  I kept generating new characters whenever I
tried to continue from a save.

Basically, the game told me that the save version was too old.  Checking
my date, I found that it was Jan 19, 1993.  I knew my clock ran slow, but
I had not realized that the game would check the date instead of looking
for some kind of stamp inside the saved game itself.

This complaint really only affects PC users.  PC clocks are notorious for
being slow, incorrect, buggy, and have a miriad of other difficulties.

Other than the fact I haven't passed the second dungeon level yet,
everything is great.

Chris Wilde


